      "observed": "REG2.1 is on +3.3V, while the MCU decoupling capacitors are on a separate +3V3 net. None of the FCC or NAVC VDD pins is connected to either rail; the only NAVC supply pin on +3V3 is VBAT.",
      "expected": "The specification says the 3.3 V rail feeds both MCUs and sensors. The MCU VDD pins should be connected to the regulated 3.3 V rail, and the +3.3V and +3V3 nets should be joined if they represent that same supply.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"REG2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\") ... ) on net \"+3.3V\""
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"276\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"19\") (pinfunction \"VDD\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3 V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Both MCUs have their VDD pins unpowered in the described connectivity, so the flight-control and navigation computers cannot operate as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE2", "FCC1", "NAVC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(FCC1-PH0)", "VREF+_FCC"],
      "observed": "The FCC crystal HSE1 is connected to FCC1.5 (PE6) and FCC1.37 (PE7), rather than the MCU's PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. The NAVC crystal HSE2 is not connected to NAVC1 at all; NAVC1.5/6 (PH0/PH1) instead connect to separate capacitor nets.",
      "expected": "Each 25 MHz HSE crystal should connect between the MCU's PH0/PH1 oscillator pins, with its load capacitors connected as required by the oscillator circuit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\")) (node (ref \"HSE1\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"33\") (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"90\") (name \"Net-(NAVC1-PH0_)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The external HSE clocks are not wired to the MCU oscillator inputs. Firmware configured to use these crystals may fail to start or fall back to a different clock, affecting timing and system operation.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["FCC1", "UART3_FCC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.48", "FCC1.73", "UART3_FCC1.3", "UART3_FCC1.4"],
      "nets": ["UART3_TX_FCC", "UART3_RX_FCC"],
      "observed": "The UART3 connector's signal pins are connected to FCC1.48 and FCC1.73, both identified as VCAP pins of the STM32H753.",
      "expected": "UART signals should use MCU UART-capable GPIO pins. VCAP pins should have the required core-regulator capacitors and must not be used as serial signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"4\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"146\") (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC1\") (pin \"3\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART3 connector cannot provide UART communication, and loading or driving the VCAP nodes may disrupt the MCU's internal core supply.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: both MCUs' VDD pins are unconnected, the HSE crystals are miswired or disconnected, and the FCC UART3 connector is routed to VCAP pins. These connectivity errors prevent the board from behaving as specified."
}

